    "text": "**Case A**\n\n- **A1 \u2013 Yes.** The seven-day search covers the whole period since publication and returned only the usual-region, stable-fingerprint requests, so the burst is the first anomalous use. This assumes the burst is misuse, which the facts strongly suggest but do not prove.\n- **A2 \u2013 Yes.** The burst (new proxy, new fingerprint, payout change) happened at 19 minutes and the check scored the account at 30 minutes without flagging it. This assumes the check can see the account's own request and change records, which is not stated.\n- **A3 \u2013 No, not by itself.** A shared payout destination fits one owner, but it equally fits a mule or attacker-controlled destination used across several accounts.\n- **A4 \u2013 Yes, weakly.** Thirty days is long enough that a redirected payout would usually have been noticed, so the silence counts a little, but it does not clear the payouts.\n- **A5 \u2013 Yes.** A new network path, a new fingerprint and payout changes minutes after a key leak are exactly what should be investigated.\n\n**Case B**\n\n- **B1 \u2013 Yes.** D has 0 chargebacks in 100 transactions against 2 in 100 for the others, with equal denominators. The difference is small and may not be meaningful.\n- **B2 \u2013 No.** A combined 5 percent is an average; unless every account sits at exactly 5 percent, at least one is above it.\n- **B3 \u2013 Yes.** The search covered all merchant accounts and found only A and the closed account. It shows no other accounts under that person's name, though it cannot rule out accounts held through nominees.\n- **B4 \u2013 Cannot tell.** Different analysts on different days is not enough; we are not told whether they worked from the same evidence or whether the second read the first note.\n- **B5 \u2013 No.** The payment has no chargeback because it was blocked as suspected fraud, not because it was clean.\n- **B6 \u2013 Yes.** Shared templates, a common descriptor pattern and settlement through the same four accounts are enough to look at them together.\n\nRESULT MF-008 | A1: Yes | A2: Yes | A3: No, not by itself | A4: Yes, weakly | A5: Yes | B1: Yes | B2: No | B3: Yes | B4: Cannot tell | B5: No | B6: Yes"
